# Fblthp, Impossibly Lost: "Draw two cards. If your library has no cards in it, you win the game." Bot1's library holds one
# card as the trigger resolves: the first draw takes it, the second draws nothing (CR 121.3), and Bot1 wins while the
# ability is resolving, before state-based actions could make Bot1 lose for the empty-library draw (the card's ruling).
# CR 104.1 ends the game immediately at the win, so Fblthp stays on the battlefield and the library stays empty.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fblthp, Impossibly Lost
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Fblthp, Impossibly Lost.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Fblthp, Impossibly Lost > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Result = Bot1 won
Bot1.Library.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot2.Life = 19
